{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 color_midi_item_by_pitch.lua\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script colors MIDI items based on their pitch bend value. The color changes from default, to orange/red for positive pitch bends, and to light blue/blue for negative pitch bends.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This is useful for preventing accidentally using MIDI items that have been pitch-bent, and spending time trying to figure out why they sound different.\par}
}
]]></description>
